tive topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear when you are in an accident."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn5le04ob03re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Simple Past Tense"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the Simple Past tense to talk about events that are finished."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Simple Past tense verbs can be regular or irregular.</br> Regular verbs end in <span class=\"strong\">-ed</span> or <span class=\"strong\">-ied</span>.</br>  Irregular verbs change in different ways.</br> For questions in the past, you use the auxiliary <span class=\"italic\">did</span> followed by the verb in the base form, like <span class=\"italic\">Did you ask ... ?</span></br> <span class=\"italic\"> Did</span> is the past form of <span class=\"italic\">to do</span>."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":9,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Simple Past Tense\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to decide\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"decided\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to copy\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"copied\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to protect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"protected\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to lose\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"lost\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to be\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was, were\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to get\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"got\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to go\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"went\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to tell\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"told\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "We got into an accident. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "We went the wrong way on Lombard Street. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "We didn't see the cable cars coming."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Quantifiers"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use a quantifier before a noun to indicate the amount or number of an item."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use quantifiers with both count and non-count nouns. </br>You can use the quantifiers below with both count and non-count nouns."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Quantifier\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"more</br> less/fewer</br> no/none</br> any /not any</br> some</br> a couple of</br> a few</br> a lot of / lots of</br> plenty of</br> enough\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"a larger number/amount</br> a smaller number/amount</br> 0</br> to ask about / say there are 0 </br> a small number/amount</br> two</br> three or four</br> a very large number/amount</br> more than you need< /br> as much as you need\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "We were in an accident with a couple of cable cars and a lot of angry tourists."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "con